#### text ####
text: Andrew split off from the rest of us and visited the Currency Museum just before it closed for the day. It's behind a security check and metal detector, which meant he got to show off his own pocketful of currency to get in. Japan has had several different currencies over the centuries, as the money was only standardized when there was a strong central authority and not in between. It also had a lot of actual gold on display and Andrew brought one home as a souvenir. (actually made of chocolate not gold)
