#### text ####
text: We were all tired and cold that evening so I suggested a super nearby restaurant, only 100m from where were staying. It was in a converted house, run by a single person (with his young kid around too), and ended up being a favourite of the trip. James especially enjoyed the unexpected cheese and mochi okonomiyaki, while I enjoyed the classic pork okonomiyaki. We liked it so much we went back a second time! They also had the rare case of an alcoholic drink that I enjoyed enough to finish, a lemon chu-hai (lemon, soda water and sochu)
