-----
alt: 
-----
css_classes: 
-----
caption: 
-----
video_link: 
#### text ####
text: Behind the shops and fancy houses was a row of tenement housing. Even by modern standards, the quarters were cramped. They were only one room with just enough space for a couple tatami and a tiny kitchen, and might have had a whole family living in them. The toilet at the end of the row was shared. We joked this was James' new kitchen.
