#### text ####
text: Teamlab Planets is in an area called Odaiba, which was built recently on reclaimed land. Unlike the narrow and crowded streets of the Tokyo that we're used to, in Odaiba the streets are wide, the sidewalks are empty and the population density is much lower. This was exemplified when we had to walk two long barren blocks to find lunch in a touristy mall with the vibes of old Tokyo, complete with reenactment performers like samurai and taiko drums. As you might guess, it wasn't my favourite neighbourhood.
